# Learn more https://docs.github.com/en/get-started/getting-started-with-git/ignoring-files

# Raster images generated by scripts/generate-assets.mjs (run: npm run generate-assets)
assets/**/*.png
assets/**/*.jpg
assets/**/*.jpeg

# ...except the ones the native build actually consumes.
#
# EAS Build prebuilds from a fresh clone and never runs the generator, so an
# ignored icon is not "regenerated later" — prebuild fails outright with
# ENOENT on ./assets/images/icon.png before it reaches signing.
#
# icon.png is additionally NOT reproducible: it is the only PNG here without an
# alpha channel, having been flattened by hand because Apple rejects
# transparent marketing icons (icon-with-alpha.bak.png is the pre-flatten
# original). Re-running the generator would put the alpha back.
#
# Exactly the files referenced by app.json and the expo-splash-screen plugin.
# Everything else the generator emits — adaptive-icon.png, splash.png, the
# .bak, assets/demo — is unreferenced and stays ignored.
!assets/images/icon.png
!assets/images/android-icon-foreground.png
!assets/images/android-icon-background.png
!assets/images/android-icon-monochrome.png
!assets/images/splash-icon.png
!assets/images/favicon.png

# dependencies
node_modules/

